@startuml

title PENA POC 01 — Digest Output Design

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam class {
  BorderColor #2F5597
  BackgroundColor #F8FBFF
  ArrowColor #444444
}

skinparam artifact {
  BorderColor #666666
  BackgroundColor #FFFCE8
}

artifact "digest-YYYYMMDD-HHMM.md" as DIGESTFILE

class DigestDocument {
  +digest_id
  +run_id
  +topic
  +created_at
  +summary_style
}

class DigestHeader {
  +title
  +topic
  +date
  +model_used
  +input_count
}

class ExecutiveSummary {
  +short_summary
  +key_takeaways
}

class DigestItem {
  +rank
  +title
  +source
  +url
  +summary
}

class TrustRelevanceBlock {
  +trust_score
  +relevance_score
  +reasons
  +uncertainty_notes
}

class SourceNotes {
  +source_name
  +source_type
  +source_reputation_note
}

class FollowUpSection {
  +recommended_questions
  +items_to_verify
  +possible_next_sources
}

class ObservabilitySummary {
  +run_id
  +prompt_version
  +model_metadata
  +warnings
  +output_paths
}

DigestDocument --> DigestHeader
DigestDocument --> ExecutiveSummary
DigestDocument --> DigestItem
DigestDocument --> FollowUpSection
DigestDocument --> ObservabilitySummary

DigestItem --> TrustRelevanceBlock
DigestItem --> SourceNotes

DigestDocument --> DIGESTFILE : rendered as Markdown

note bottom of DigestDocument
The digest is the first user-facing artifact.
It should be useful before any web UI exists.
end note

note right of ObservabilitySummary
POC 01 includes operational metadata
so the human can inspect how the result was produced.
end note

@enduml
